course: dictionary
lesson: 799
title: Beetles and their six legs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A beetle is an insect with a hard, shiny back. The words around a word give you clues to its meaning. «Every insect has 6 legs: ants, beetles, bees, ladybirds and grasshoppers all walk on 6 legs.» Beetles are in a list of insects, so a beetle is an insect with 6 legs.
explain: The hard back is not just a shell. «A beetle's wing cases meet in a straight line down its back» tells you that the hard back covers the wings, which is why most beetles can still fly.
explain: Some words give you a clue about which kind of beetle you mean. In «a stag beetle», the word stag tells you the name of one kind. Beetle is the big family name, and the words before it tell you which member of the family.
fact: A beetle is an insect with a hard, shiny back.
fact: Like all insects, a beetle has 6 legs, 3 body parts and 2 feelers.
fact: The hard back is a pair of wing cases that cover thin wings, so most beetles can fly.
fact: There are more kinds of beetle than of any other animal.
fact: Ladybirds (ladybugs) are beetles, and beetles help break down dead plants.
exercise: «Like all insects, a beetle has six legs, three body parts and two feelers.» How many legs does a beetle have? | 8 | 10 | *6 | 4
exercise: Which of these animals is a beetle? | A grasshopper with long jumping legs | A snail | A spider | *A ladybird
exercise: «A beetle's wing cases meet in a straight line down its back.» What covers a beetle's thin wings? | Six legs | *Hard wing cases | Three body parts | Two feelers
test: «Every insect has 6 legs: ants, beetles, bees, ladybirds and grasshoppers all walk on 6 legs.» Which word in the list is NOT a beetle? | *Ant | Ladybird again, because ladybirds are beetles | Beetle | Ladybird
test: In the phrase «a stag beetle», what does the word stag tell you? | It is a kind of bird | *It is a kind of beetle | It means the beetle is dead | It is a kind of fly
exam: Jayden says a beetle has eight legs because it is an animal. Is he right, and why? | Yes, because every bug has eight legs | Yes, because all animals have eight legs | *No, all insects have six legs, so a beetle has six | No, because beetles have no legs at all
